WEBVTT

00:04.000 --> 00:07.260
Sa-chan,
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hI've brought you a change of clotheso
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hAfter all, we're friendso

00:04.000 --> 00:04.040
From Komari

00:14.120 --> 00:15.680
Did something happen?

00:15.680 --> 00:16.840
You were in such a hurry.

00:16.840 --> 00:18.500
Oh, no.

00:18.500 --> 00:20.290
It's nothing.

00:20.290 --> 00:22.280
I can't let her worry.

00:24.360 --> 00:28.150
This world was created by someone who made a wish.

00:28.500 --> 00:33.460
And if the creator of this world's wish is granted, it'll disappear.

00:34.780 --> 00:37.000
That's a bit far-fetched, is it not?

00:37.620 --> 00:38.910
It's happened before.

00:38.910 --> 00:40.350
Something like this.

00:41.700 --> 00:43.000
I understand.

00:43.000 --> 00:46.050
So I'll believe in those words of yours.

00:46.050 --> 00:48.120
Thank you.

00:48.120 --> 00:52.070
Since there is no logical explanation to this, I cannot help it.

00:52.070 --> 00:58.850
So? Do you have any idea regarding this world’s creator’s identity, or this world’s purpose?

00:58.850 --> 01:00.930
Well, not yet at least...

01:02.320 --> 01:06.410
It appears that I'll have to continue my life as a shut-in for a while longer.

01:07.230 --> 01:11.940
I am sorry to impose on you, but I shall be in your care once again.

01:11.940 --> 01:13.950
L-Likewise.

01:16.540 --> 01:18.260
A marriage proposal?

01:18.260 --> 01:22.990
This is why you're such a hopeless case!

01:38.260 --> 01:45.100
Presented By Refrain Subs!

01:48.770 --> 01:54.650
Since being alone was tough, the two of us held hands.

01:55.150 --> 02:01.160
The two of us were lonely, so we all stood in a circle and joined hands.

02:01.120 --> 02:09.370
I'm sure that's where we will gather our strength.

02:09.290 --> 02:14.340
Enough to stand up to any dream.

02:14.210 --> 02:16.970
Fly high towards the sky,

02:16.630 --> 02:21.140
Kick off the ground and send your voice to the heavens,

02:20.840 --> 02:26.180
Until you overcome those painful days.

02:25.970 --> 02:31.310
I'll never forget your voice, and I'll never forget your tears.

02:27.930 --> 02:27.980
The First Annual Make Kyousuke Chuckle Championships

02:30.940 --> 02:38.280
The future that we call "hope" begins now.

02:38.030 --> 02:49.080
Your feet will continue to step onward, even when the time of grief comes.

02:54.400 --> 02:56.380
The creator's wish, huh?

02:56.960 --> 03:01.820
I'm sure Sasasegawa-san has an idea as to why she's transforming into a black cat.

03:04.180 --> 03:06.600
Wait, Rin isn't here?

03:06.600 --> 03:09.050
Come to think of it, neither are the others.

03:17.830 --> 03:23.930
The phone you're trying to call is currently turned off or out of service...

03:24.790 --> 03:27.970
There's no way everyone would skip.

03:28.620 --> 03:31.000
Riki, is there something you're hiding from me?

03:31.920 --> 03:35.920
We've been together for so long that I'm able to tell when something's off.

03:36.580 --> 03:40.110
If I tell him, he might disappear.

03:41.560 --> 03:44.260
I'm sorry, but right now...

03:44.260 --> 03:45.050
I understand.

03:45.560 --> 03:48.750
Tell me whenever you're ready.

03:48.750 --> 03:51.670
You can always count on me.

03:51.670 --> 03:53.830
Yeah, thanks.

03:58.820 --> 04:01.280
What is she doing?

04:01.280 --> 04:04.560
And what's up with that apron?

04:04.560 --> 04:06.740
Ah, welcome home.

04:06.740 --> 04:09.850
The chinjao rosu is almost ready.

04:12.520 --> 04:13.900
Let's eat.

04:13.900 --> 04:15.340
Let us eat.

04:16.260 --> 04:17.000
This is delicious!

04:17.320 --> 04:20.400
This has to be the best chinjao rosu I've ever eaten.

04:22.200 --> 04:25.680
There's a lot of it, so eat as much as you want.

04:26.520 --> 04:27.430
Well then, I'll...

04:29.620 --> 04:31.310
The lettuce is nice and crispy too.

04:31.310 --> 04:34.770
Wait, why am I getting so happy over something like this?!

04:34.770 --> 04:37.900
Well, you seem to be enjoying yourself.

04:37.900 --> 04:40.390
I am having fun, but...

04:40.390 --> 04:44.840
When I think about what you said earlier, I just feel so pathetic.

04:44.840 --> 04:47.860
It's important to have these sort of experiences, too.

04:47.860 --> 04:51.280
If you're serious all the time, you'll never be able to enjoy yourself.

04:51.560 --> 04:55.150
Especially when you work so hard, you'll certainly—

04:55.760 --> 04:58.900
Who are you calling hard-working?

04:58.900 --> 05:00.200
I'm sorry.

05:01.260 --> 05:02.300
Anyway...

05:03.370 --> 05:04.220
That weir—I mean elegant apron...

05:07.040 --> 05:08.890
It's pretty, isn't it?

05:08.890 --> 05:11.540
I borrowed it from over there.

05:13.300 --> 05:14.880
I wonder if it's Rin's?

05:14.880 --> 05:17.020
I thought you hated cats.

05:17.570 --> 05:19.080
I do hate them.

05:20.100 --> 05:23.140
But aprons won't run away.

05:25.030 --> 05:26.150
Did something happen?

05:26.630 --> 05:30.720
I didn't picture you as someone who truly hates cats.

05:33.040 --> 05:35.020
It's an old story.

05:35.020 --> 05:38.220
I once owned a cat.

05:39.000 --> 05:40.380
It was a black cat.

05:43.420 --> 05:45.540
Would you like to come home with me?

05:48.550 --> 05:51.540
It would always cry in the middle of the night.

05:51.540 --> 05:56.290
When I wasn't around, it would start looking for me.

05:56.290 --> 05:58.180
It was a lot of trouble.

05:58.680 --> 06:03.350
But even in those hard times, there were a lot of happy times

06:04.220 --> 06:09.310
One year later, our family decided to move away.

06:10.520 --> 06:15.520
On that fateful day, I couldn't find the cat anywhere.

06:16.380 --> 06:19.000
I looked everywhere for it.

06:19.000 --> 06:19.980
But just like that,

06:19.980 --> 06:23.260
I never saw it again.

06:25.940 --> 06:27.670
When a house cat goes out into the wild,

06:27.670 --> 06:31.700
the chances for its survival are about 1 in 3.

06:32.640 --> 06:35.750
I'm sure it died somewhere.

06:36.330 --> 06:39.880
I'm sure it came to hate me.

06:41.010 --> 06:42.910
It’s not that she hates cats.

06:43.510 --> 06:45.360
She just has no other choice but to hate them.

06:46.680 --> 06:49.270
Thank you for telling me.

06:53.650 --> 06:58.440
I feel like Sasasegawa-san subconsciously created this world

06:58.440 --> 07:01.520
with her strong desire to meet Kuroneko again.

07:02.800 --> 07:06.280
Sasasegawa-san, is there a wish you want to come true?

07:06.280 --> 07:08.110
Why are you asking that so suddenly?

07:08.110 --> 07:12.840
Well, I was just wondering what kind of strong wish you'd need to create this world.

07:15.720 --> 07:17.340
Now that you mention it...

07:17.340 --> 07:19.040
Do you really have none?

07:19.040 --> 07:22.730
That's right, you like Kengo, don't you?

07:22.730 --> 07:24.180
What?!

07:24.180 --> 07:26.140
Oh, am I wrong?

07:26.140 --> 07:29.690
W-well, you're not mistaken...

07:29.690 --> 07:34.600
Could it be that your strongest wish in this world has something to do with him?

07:35.280 --> 07:37.150
I guess so.

07:37.150 --> 07:41.540
To be honest, I'd like to talk to Miyazawa-sama alone even in this world.

07:41.540 --> 07:44.170
That would be wonderful.

07:44.170 --> 07:47.240
Then, why don't you go talk to him, in private?

07:47.500 --> 07:48.290
Huh?!

07:48.320 --> 07:51.820
I think it's important to let him know about this world.

07:51.820 --> 07:54.050
First off, you should explain the situation to him.

07:54.050 --> 07:55.220
The situation?

07:55.220 --> 07:56.640
What do you mean by that?

07:56.640 --> 07:59.090
Like I said, tell him about this world.

07:59.090 --> 08:00.600
Why does it have to be me?

08:00.600 --> 08:01.980
That's impossible!

08:01.980 --> 08:05.350
Not to mention that I'll transform into a cat in front of him.

08:05.350 --> 08:08.270
You'll never know until you try.

08:08.270 --> 08:11.420
Maybe your words will be able to reach him.

08:11.420 --> 08:13.020
That may be true...

08:13.020 --> 08:16.510
But I really can't talk to Miyazawa-sama.

08:16.510 --> 08:20.230
I cannot face him in this pathetic state.

08:20.600 --> 08:22.040
You'll be fine.

08:22.040 --> 08:23.740
You're not pathetic at all.

08:23.740 --> 08:29.630
You're such a hard worker and your cooking is delicious.

08:29.630 --> 08:31.960
And most of all, you're cute.

08:32.460 --> 08:34.810
That's why you'll be fine.

08:34.810 --> 08:38.150
Um, well, your hand is...

08:38.150 --> 08:40.140
I'm sorry, I didn't...

08:41.660 --> 08:44.070
I guess there is no helping it.

08:44.070 --> 08:46.020
If you are willing to go that far.

08:46.020 --> 08:46.970
Really?

08:46.970 --> 08:50.200
It's fine for me to tell him about my situation, right?

08:50.200 --> 08:51.070
Yeah.

08:52.790 --> 08:54.490
Are you sure that's enough?

08:54.490 --> 08:56.200
What do you mean by that?

08:56.200 --> 08:59.770
Well, if you muster up the courage to be alone with him,

08:59.770 --> 09:01.430
you might as well confess.

09:02.100 --> 09:06.500
Hold on, there is no way I would let myself get ridiculed like that!

09:06.880 --> 09:09.270
What do you mean, ridiculed?

09:24.640 --> 09:27.610
It was that dream again.

09:27.610 --> 09:29.220
Good morning.

09:32.220 --> 09:33.500
You're sure up early.

09:33.500 --> 09:35.420
So you're finally awake.

09:35.420 --> 09:37.520
Does anything look off?

09:37.520 --> 09:40.640
Don't worry, you look the same as usual.

09:41.500 --> 09:43.390
If it's the same as usual, it's not good enough.

09:43.390 --> 09:44.750
I'll do it again.

09:48.170 --> 09:51.710
It really was impossible!

09:52.610 --> 09:53.840
Sasasegawa-san!

10:06.410 --> 10:08.760
Did he not understand you?

10:08.760 --> 10:10.100
I don't know.

10:10.100 --> 10:12.900
I fled right away.

10:13.560 --> 10:14.940
Riki.

10:14.940 --> 10:16.560
What was up with that?

10:16.560 --> 10:18.360
There was no one else in the room.

10:18.360 --> 10:20.170
Other than the cat.

10:21.960 --> 10:23.120
Miyazawa-sama.

10:23.120 --> 10:24.050
Huh?

10:24.050 --> 10:26.920
Wasn't that Sasasegawa's voice?

10:26.920 --> 10:27.700
Don't tell me...

10:28.760 --> 10:30.570
It's Sasasegawa-san.

10:30.570 --> 10:33.820
In this world, Sasasegawa-san has turned into a cat.

10:33.820 --> 10:35.040
What did you say?!

10:35.040 --> 10:36.690
Miyazawa-sama.

10:37.550 --> 10:41.090
It is I, Sasasegawa Sasami.

10:41.090 --> 10:44.350
Sasasegawa has really...

10:44.350 --> 10:46.100
Thanks goodness, with this...

10:46.100 --> 10:47.090
Miyazawa-sama!

10:49.060 --> 10:50.310
W-What the—?

10:50.310 --> 10:51.590
Miyazawa-sama!

10:55.870 --> 10:57.110
Riki!

11:01.400 --> 11:06.020
I was wrong about everything.

11:06.020 --> 11:07.550
What's going on?

11:07.550 --> 11:09.080
What happened to Miyazawa-sama?

11:09.860 --> 11:13.860
They disappear from this world when they learn about...

11:13.860 --> 11:15.210
Are you serious?

11:15.210 --> 11:16.540
Then, could it be...

11:17.590 --> 11:18.500
Kamikita-san!

11:25.920 --> 11:27.980
Why did you not tell me about it?

11:29.080 --> 11:31.660
I didn't want you to worry.

11:32.600 --> 11:38.000
I appreciate your concern, but please inform me of such matters.

11:38.000 --> 11:41.860
In baseball and softball, the most important thing is teamwork.

11:41.860 --> 11:45.450
Two is better than one, obviously.

11:57.310 --> 11:58.420
The outside is...

12:14.150 --> 12:15.480
It's starting to falter.

12:16.720 --> 12:21.080
The master's power is starting to weaken, and the world is starting to fall apart.

12:27.590 --> 12:29.480
Hey, that might be the exit.

12:29.480 --> 12:30.540
Is that really true?

12:30.540 --> 12:31.470
Wait!

12:31.470 --> 12:36.020
If you leave like that, you might stay a cat forever.

12:36.020 --> 12:37.520
What should I do, then?

12:37.520 --> 12:40.960
We have to find the creator of this world and fulfill his wish.

12:42.880 --> 12:44.420
What will you do?

12:45.540 --> 12:47.860
I won't leave yet.

12:47.860 --> 12:52.680
I can't leave you by yourself. I'll stay with you until the end.

12:54.090 --> 12:57.690
I'm fine without you worrying about me.

12:57.690 --> 12:59.810
But, thank you for staying with me.

12:59.810 --> 13:00.680
Yep.

13:05.280 --> 13:06.990
It's quiet, isn't it?

13:06.990 --> 13:08.690
Yeah.

13:08.690 --> 13:11.830
Where do you think they are?

13:11.830 --> 13:13.700
If we don't find the creator,

13:13.700 --> 13:15.460
we won't know what their wish.

13:19.460 --> 13:24.970
If the creator of this world wants us to fulfill their wish, then they would need to meet us.

13:24.970 --> 13:30.720
If they're unable to do that, what's their true purpose, and is it inevitable?

13:42.720 --> 13:44.700
You can never get enough, can you?

13:44.700 --> 13:49.000
Your chinjao rosu is just so delicious.

13:51.560 --> 13:54.040
I wonder how long this world can hold up.

13:55.380 --> 13:59.800
If this world disappears, what will become of us?

13:59.800 --> 14:02.530
We will most likely disappear forever.

14:03.320 --> 14:05.510
Let's go look again tomorrow.

14:05.920 --> 14:06.960
We might find a hint or something.

14:06.960 --> 14:08.780
That's enough.

14:09.270 --> 14:11.340
Let's go back to our original world.

14:11.340 --> 14:13.430
But then you will...

14:13.430 --> 14:17.640
It's better to be stuck being a cat than to disappear forever.

14:20.290 --> 14:25.130
It might not be that bad to be your pet cat.

14:29.030 --> 14:33.120
Is it really fine to go back to our original world like this?

14:33.510 --> 14:36.780
To go back without fulfilling the creator's wish?

14:43.510 --> 14:45.370
Want to come home with me?

14:47.800 --> 14:47.840
I'm here!

14:50.610 --> 14:51.580
What was that?

14:53.140 --> 14:54.220
Sasasegawa-san?

14:58.420 --> 15:00.540
Why didn't I notice it until now?

15:00.540 --> 15:03.020
It wasn't just a dream.

15:03.020 --> 15:05.540
It was a fragment of your memory.

15:08.500 --> 15:10.100
So you are the master.

15:15.220 --> 15:17.070
Want to come home with me?

15:18.620 --> 15:20.470
I shall name you Kuro.

15:20.470 --> 15:22.330
So from now on, your name is Kuro.

15:23.420 --> 15:25.270
Kuro, Kuro, Kuro, Kuro.

15:28.740 --> 15:31.970
Hey now, don't nibble my finger.

15:41.930 --> 15:44.030
Oh, it's a cat.

15:44.030 --> 15:45.810
You don't seem too well, kitty.

15:46.810 --> 15:51.160
I-It has nothing to do with me. After all, I hate cats.

15:52.050 --> 15:57.070
Even though you were able to meet Sasasegawa-san again, she didn't realize it was you.

15:57.980 --> 16:02.420
By showing me your memories, what is your wish?

16:04.440 --> 16:06.250
The black cat is the master?

16:06.250 --> 16:08.550
Yeah, it's Kuro.

16:08.550 --> 16:10.820
The cat you kept as your pet when you were a child.

16:10.820 --> 16:12.600
How do you know that name?

16:12.600 --> 16:14.550
Kuro told me.

16:14.550 --> 16:17.270
Kuro lived on as a stray cat.

16:17.270 --> 16:19.720
You even met Kuro again at school.

16:20.780 --> 16:22.610
Is that so?

16:22.610 --> 16:25.910
So then, what did Kuro wish for?

16:25.910 --> 16:29.680
Does Kuro want to see revenge on me for abandoning it?

16:31.280 --> 16:34.540
I don't know, but it's possible that it wants to meet you.

16:35.060 --> 16:37.070
There's no time.

16:37.070 --> 16:38.050
Kuro is...

16:38.050 --> 16:41.240
Kuro is starting to run out of power.

16:41.240 --> 16:43.840
These will be his last moments in this world.

16:47.230 --> 16:48.550
I understand.

16:51.910 --> 16:54.070
Am I not going to transform?

17:06.730 --> 17:08.350
Wait a minute.

17:09.460 --> 17:14.900
It seems Kuro doesn't want to meet me as I can't go any further than this.

17:16.480 --> 17:19.160
You wanted to meet Sasasegawa-san, right?

17:19.160 --> 17:21.350
You wanted to tell her something, didn't you?

17:21.840 --> 17:24.160
That's enough...

17:40.930 --> 17:43.370
Looks like this really was the exit.

17:43.370 --> 17:44.910
Is this really all right?

17:44.910 --> 17:47.060
Yeah, thanks for all you've done so far.

17:48.140 --> 17:49.400
I understand.

17:49.400 --> 17:50.810
Well then...

17:56.450 --> 17:57.610
What's the meaning of this?

17:57.610 --> 17:59.900
I'm going to stay here.

17:59.900 --> 18:02.830
I'm the one that took her in and left her behind.

18:02.830 --> 18:04.410
It's all my fault.

18:04.410 --> 18:06.460
In the end, I have to take responsibility.

18:06.460 --> 18:07.730
This is wrong!

18:07.730 --> 18:09.710
Why does it have to be just you in the end?

18:09.710 --> 18:11.040
If you want to meet Kuro,

18:11.040 --> 18:12.130
I'll come with you!

18:12.130 --> 18:14.170
What will I do if you don't make it back?!

18:15.350 --> 18:19.290
If you go back, you'll be safe.

18:19.290 --> 18:20.000
But—

18:20.000 --> 18:21.200
That's why even if it's just you...

18:21.200 --> 18:23.320
It's fine, don't worry.

18:24.600 --> 18:25.250
That's why...

18:26.020 --> 18:27.320
Goodbye.

18:29.300 --> 18:30.400
Wait!

18:32.520 --> 18:34.260
Sasasegawa-san!

18:35.480 --> 18:39.980
Why did this have to happen? It's too selfish.

18:42.910 --> 18:45.600
We have to do this together.

18:48.280 --> 18:49.250
I will!

18:54.120 --> 18:54.880
This place...

18:56.340 --> 18:57.980
Sasasegawa-san.

18:59.130 --> 19:00.590
You, how?

19:01.080 --> 19:05.100
As I thought, there's no meaning if I don't get out with Sasasegawa-san.

19:06.720 --> 19:08.630
I don't believe it.

19:08.630 --> 19:11.980
To just crush my final wish like that.

19:12.570 --> 19:13.470
I'm sorry.

19:13.470 --> 19:15.650
You don't need to apologize.

19:16.110 --> 19:20.860
Because in the end, there wasn't anything I could do alone.

19:23.000 --> 19:26.600
Let's go to Kuro's place together, once again.

19:27.540 --> 19:31.910
There may be some things you're unable to do alone, but there's so much you can do when you're together.

19:31.910 --> 19:36.800
Even though we're weak alone, you're the one that taught me that.

19:44.260 --> 19:45.500
Sasasegawa-san.

19:48.280 --> 19:49.970
It's me.

19:49.970 --> 19:52.500
I want to see you, Kuro.

19:54.420 --> 19:56.610
Kuro, Kuro!

19:57.470 --> 19:58.560
Kuro!

19:58.560 --> 20:03.020
Jeez, where have you been?
You've been worrying me sick.

20:03.670 --> 20:05.660
Don't meow me.

20:05.660 --> 20:08.700
Come on, say the words Mama loves to hear.

20:10.120 --> 20:10.160
I'm here!

20:10.420 --> 20:12.540
I'm here.

20:16.910 --> 20:19.710
My words.

20:20.530 --> 20:24.100
Kuro always remembered it.

20:29.140 --> 20:30.860
This was where we met, wasn't it?

20:37.120 --> 20:40.360
Kuro, I'm sorry.

20:47.080 --> 20:49.830
Why did it have to run away from everyone?

20:50.310 --> 20:52.530
Is it because my words didn't reach?

20:52.530 --> 20:56.330
No, it just didn't want to hear what we had to say.

20:56.590 --> 20:57.710
Above all else.

20:58.440 --> 21:00.410
You want to play?

21:00.410 --> 21:02.020
Don't you?

21:02.020 --> 21:04.300
Mama will play with you.

21:04.600 --> 21:07.750
Even though it was full of sad things.

21:08.370 --> 21:12.830
But in the end, it finally got its reward.

21:12.830 --> 21:14.140
Isn't that great?

21:14.760 --> 21:17.470
That's the whole purpose of this world.

21:22.440 --> 21:24.400
Kuro, Kuro, Kuro, Kuro.

21:26.550 --> 21:28.560
Kuro, Kuro, Kuro.

21:28.560 --> 21:32.740
Hey now, don't nibble my finger.

21:32.740 --> 21:34.660
Kuro, Kuro, Kuro, Kuro.

21:37.940 --> 21:41.800
Kuro, isn't it about time for you to sleep?

21:53.130 --> 21:55.970
Bye bye, Kuro.

22:09.910 --> 22:21.070
Under those scarlet clouds, two of my memories start to drift far away.

22:21.430 --> 22:28.460
Among the echoes of a bell chime, we both take a piece.

22:28.180 --> 22:32.710
I hope the sun will be out tomorrow.

22:32.390 --> 22:37.090
I wonder if we can make it beyond the stars?

22:35.920 --> 22:41.480
You're supposed to smile after you cry.

22:36.820 --> 22:43.890
As I walk, I look up at the sky and see a single light.

22:42.270 --> 22:44.580
Isn't that right, Kuro?

22:43.570 --> 22:48.850
Even if I'm all alone above the moon,

22:48.620 --> 22:56.610
I'll run towards the end of this spiral.

22:56.710 --> 23:03.160
You said that I would be able to smile after I cried.

23:02.930 --> 23:08.750
I won't ever forget our journey.

23:08.350 --> 23:14.500
I'll cast a spell so you won't forget, and I won't say goodbye.

23:14.270 --> 23:20.840
You'll be able to walk forward again someday

23:27.300 --> 23:31.060
Episode 6

23:27.300 --> 23:31.060
A Small World Someone Wished For

23:31.090 --> 23:41.070
Episode 7

23:31.090 --> 23:41.070
Kanata's Secret

23:32.480 --> 23:36.870
Naoe Riki, you're a person who can't live without his friends, aren't you?

23:36.870 --> 23:40.280
Futaki-san, what are you hiding under that cold facade?
